  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great North Road Upgrade Zambia section of the North South Corridor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project consists of the upgrade with only marginal changes to the existing alignment of about 372 km of the single carriageway Zambian Great North Road (GNR), also known as Trunk Road number 2 (T2), linking Mpika and Nakonde in the Muchinga Province, in North-Eastern Zambia at the border to Tanzania. The GNR is one of the six international trunk roads in Zambia with strong regional importance, as it forms part in particular of the North-South Corridor. The road carries significant international cargo and bulk commodities. In addition the project includes Technical Assistance</narrative>
  </description>
